    "en": {
      "shared_perspectives": "German media from the left, centre and right uniformly stress that the accelerating energy transition is driving a sharp rise in household and industrial energy prices, with repeated references to IW studies warning that new gas-heating installations could double heating costs. All sides agree that expanding the electricity grid and building large-scale storage, whether battery, hydrogen or pumped-hydro, are indispensable to accommodate the planned growth of wind and solar capacity. At the same time, there is a shared concern that the speed of coal phase-out and the reliability of the future energy mix must be calibrated to safeguard German industry's global competitiveness.",
